well, what was far and away my best game just came to an end.

i was playing a Female Elven Wizard and explored down to the oracle
without anything out of the ordinary
happening (aside from finding a huge surplus of scrolls of enchant
armor and weapon when clearing out a bookstore, which i promptly used
on my staff and cloak, perhaps unwisely).Then i decided to double back
and explore the mines.

There was a close call with a fire ant on Mines lvl 2 (i think i was
only XP 7 at the time) but i survived it. Found and ID'd a wand of
poly on mines lvl3.

My real luck came in Mine Town, though. I came across a bones file
(Here lies Darren, killed by a vampire) with a magic marker. Took care
of the vampire with judicious wand of magic missilling. I then
promptly
blanked my blessed spellbook of force bult in the fountain and tried
my luck at writing a spellbook of identify.

worked on the first try!

so i locked myself in a shop with all my stuff and all Darren's stuff
and just kept casting identify over and over (with an 83% chance of
fail). Turned out Darren was also toting around a bag of holding,
scroll of charging and a magic lamp (all cursed). So  diluted some
potions in the fountain, prayed to anhur and blesssed first a scroll
of RC and then the freshly uncursed lamp. Exploring the other shops I
found gauntlets of power (never seen them before) and a second magic
lamp(!).

So I used my first lamp to wish for SDSM. I also had enough gold to
make one good offer to the priest. So all told, my AC is now down to
-15.

I decided to take my first stab at polypiling. piled up all my
spellbooks and all my rings and zapped the poly wand a couple of
times. Came out of it with Spellbooks of Fireball, Magic Missile and
Charm Monster! Sure those spells will come in handy later. I also
(entirely by accident) caught my kitten Cinders in one of those poly
blasts, turning him into an Energy Vortex. I felt bad at first, but he
seemed to have a grand old time sucking things up and shocking them.

Cinders the Vortex and I cleared out mines end and then hung out by
the altar in minetown for a little bit making offerings. Eventually
anhur was pleased enough to give me magicbane. shortly thereafter, i
lost my +4 Cloak of MR by trying to enchant it further. oh well, I
tossed on Darren's +2 oilskin cloak and carried on my way. Thanks
again Darren!

So I carried on and hit sokoban (even though i already had the BoH and
reflection). It was worth a second bag of holding and a few other
treats. Time well spent.

Then, between the quest entrance (i wasn't high enough level) and
medusa i came across a lawful temple. without thinking I sacrficed a
dragon i had just slain, converting the altar to Anhur. of course,
this didn't make the priest happy. i thought he was going to
instadeath me, but i guess that doesn't happen when you convert? (i
remember being instadeathed in mine town once early on, and that gave
me a healthy fear of priests.)

instead, he quaffed a curse potion of gain level. so, feeling
confident, i tracked him up to the previous level, killed him and took
his +5 robe. so all was well again on the armor front (AC: -23).

a few levels lower I got swarmed by big monsters and had to resort to
Charm Monstering. So I now have an Aleax, a Red Dragon and a Black
Dragon to replace cinders (who lived a long and happy life as an
energy
vortex before being killed off-camera sometime shortly after the quest
entrance; my sad feeling has not entirely passed).

With this entourage in tow, I made it down as far as Medusa. Then
turned around to do the quest for the first time ever. Kitted out as I
was, I actually found the quest to be disappointingly easy. I don't
think there was a single point where I thought I was in real danger.

I have to admit that I was surprised to see my spells starting to fade
from memory. I had never lived long enough for that to happen before!

After the quest, I trekked down to the castle (the furthest into the
dungeon I had ever been previously) but, upon arriving, realized that
i had somehow lost the empty frost horn i was saving for the
occassion. Ah well, I thought, no big deal. I put on my ring of
levitation (and my amulet of breathing for good measure) and took the
moat around to the back door.

But then, foolishly, after crossing the moat, i took my ring off so as
to put my ring of regen back on... and promptly fell down a trap door
into the Valley of the Dead.

I went exploring for the upstair (not realizing that it was just five
steps in the other direction!) and found myself swarmed by annoying
but non-threatening monsters. so i hacked and slashed my way along,
still looking for the stairs, when suddenly i found myself double
teamed by Yeenoghu and Juiblex. I was engulfed and sickened and
heavily damaged. Used my unicorn horn to cure myself and then prayed
to try and recover my hit points. big mistake.

so then anhur was pissed at me and i was at seven (SEVEN!) hitpoints.

So, i swallowed my pride and engraved the E-word for the first time
this game. eventually i healed back up and recovered my mana. i then
engaged in a very morally suspect strategy of running into a crowd of
undead and casting charm monster, then running a few more steps and
casting again. by this method i was able to keep a couple of steps
ahead of the two demon lords and eventually find the upstair. so i ran
back up, leaving my legion of loving undead behind.

Yeenoghu followed me, by Juiblex was left behind. Thus separated, they
were much easier to deal with. There happened to be a cockatrice
hanging out by the rear entrance to the castle, so i killed it, picked
it up, and whacked Yeenie with it. Thus leaving a very ugly statue at
the bottom of the kings moat.

carefully leaving my ring of levitation on this time, i cleared out
the castle and won a wand of wishing with three charges for my effort.
i promptly wished for another magic marker (my first one having dried
out) and wrote a couple of scrolls of charging (one for the marker,
one for the wand). i then proceeded to wish for everything my heart
could desire. i used up all the wishes in the wand, but still had my
blessed magic lamp as a light source and likely wish in reserve.

i then, with very little trouble, dispatched Juiblex, cleared out
vlad's tower and explored all the way down to the bottom of gehennom
(paying off the demons along the way). as i passed through Orcus Town
on the way down, i waved a cheery hello at Orcus and gave it hardly
another thought.

When i reached the bottom level, it took me almost two hours to track
down the vibrating square. but i finally found it, marked it, and then
went to sleep.

woke up the next morning (yesterday) and thought, "i'll just climb
back up to the start of the tower before work."

But then, as I was passing back through Orcus Town, Orcus decided to
be a huge jerk and summon Demogorgon. I found myself in a very similar
situation to my earlier close call. double teamed by two demons, one
who could deal real damage to me and one who could sicken me.

Demogorgon sickened me once; i cured it with the horn and then ran for
the up stair. unfortunately, Orcus beat me to it. i quickly found
myself sickened again, blinded (by i don't remember what) and badly
beaten. I engraved the E-word for the second time and the demons
backed off one square and started throwing harmless spells at me.

I cast extra healing because i was at 22 hit points. In retrospect, I
think that casting healing while sick may have been one of the
mistakes that killed me. I got 52 points out of the heal, but never
ended up losing another hitpoint, so it was arguably unnecessary.

My next move was to apply my unicorn horn. It cured my blindness. So I
applied it again and, to my horror, it still did not cure my sickness.
Instead it brought back the one point CON that i hadn't even realised
had been drained. So I applied again and it fired a blank. DYWYPI?


